    "basic_qualifications": "- 7+ years of data engineering experience<br/>- Experience with data modeling, warehousing and building ETL pipelines<br/>- Experience with SQL<br/>- Experience in at least one modern scripting or programming language, such as Python, Java, Scala, or NodeJS<br/>- Experience mentoring team members on best practices<br/>- Experience building data products incrementally and integrating and managing data sets from multiple sources<br/>- Knowledge of professional software engineering & best practices for full software development life cycle, including coding standards, software architectures, code reviews, source control management, continuous deployments, testing, and operational excellence<br/>- Experience communicating with users, other technical teams, and management to collect requirements, describe data modeling decisions and data engineering strategy",
    "business_category": "finance",
    "city": "Seattle",
    "company_name": "Amazon.com Services LLC",
    "country_code": "USA",
    "description": "Amazon's Internal Audit organization touches every part of the business \u2014 from Stores to AWS to subsidiaries \u2014 and relies on accurate, timely data to identify and manage risk at scale. The Data Analytics Infrastructure (DAI) team within Internal Audit is looking for a Data Engineer to own the pipelines, data models, and platforms that put data-driven insight directly into the hands of auditors and analysts. This is not a greenfield build. The team already operates a production data lake with hundreds of tables and terabytes of data flowing daily, and that data cannot stop flowing while you modernize and improve what exists. This is also a breadth role: rather than going deep on a single domain, you will work with data from across the entire Amazon enterprise, learning new businesses and figuring out how their data can support audit objectives. You will lead the data lake modernization effort, build self-service analytics capabilities layered with AI, and ensure data quality that Internal Audit's partners can trust.<br/><br/>Key job responsibilities<br/>- Own the architecture of Internal Audit's Redshift-based data lake \u2014 hundreds of tables, terabytes of data in production \u2014 and lead its modernization by evaluating and adopting technologies that improve performance and the end-user experience without disrupting existing data flows.<br/>- Develop AI-powered tools and contribute to the team's platform so that auditors can find, access, and query data through self-service, turning prior audit work into reusable knowledge and removing engineering bottlenecks.<br/>- Provide technical leadership by owning critical-path code and designs, delegating work across the team, mentoring junior engineers, and staying current with industry trends to ensure the team uses the best available technology.<br/>- Design and build ETL pipelines that acquire data from across Amazon's businesses, ensuring each dataset is appropriately secured, modeled for its use case, and maintained on the right lifecycle \u2014 whether it supports a one-time engagement or ongoing audit needs.<br/>- Build and maintain data quality monitoring infrastructure to detect issues in source data and internal ETL processes, escalating upstream problems and protecting the trust Internal Audit's partners place in our data.<br/><br/><br/>A day in the life<br/>You might start the morning triaging a data quality alert on a high-demand dataset, then move into a design review for a new pipeline that will bring in data from a business line the team hasn't worked with before. After lunch you could be writing SQL to prototype a new data model, pairing with a teammate on a tricky ETL optimization, or meeting with an audit team to understand an upcoming engagement and what data they will need. You will also spend time evaluating how generative AI tools can automate repetitive work and improve how auditors interact with the team's data and knowledge assets.<br/><br/>About the team<br/>The Data Analytics Infrastructure team is a small group of data engineers \u2014 you would be the fifth \u2014 inside Amazon's Internal Audit organization, which sits within Finance. Our mission is to put data-driven insight directly into the hands of every Internal Audit member. We build the big data foundation, layer self-service analytics and AI on top, and manage the full data lifecycle so auditors can find answers without waiting on an engineer. What sets us apart is our scope: we work with data from Amazon retail, AWS, corporate functions, and subsidiaries, which means you are constantly learning new businesses. The broader Data Analytics org around us includes business intelligence engineers, data scientists, and applied scientists, giving you close partners across the analytical spectrum.",
